                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>11.786213,54.699475,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Lolland Footprints and Fish Fence</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 54.73 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 11.42<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Denmark/thumb/ancient-footprints-4.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Two sets of human footprints and some Stone Age fishing gear a so-called fishing fence, a tool that dates back to around 3,000 B.C.  Recently discovered in a dried up fjord, or inlet, on the island of...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
